    "question": "I run 12 miles in 90 minutes. What is my average speed in miles per hour?",
    "gold": "8",
    "answer": "First convert 90 minutes to hours: 90 minutes / 60 minutes/hours = <<90/60=1.5>>1.5 hours.\nIn 1 hour, I run 12 miles / 1.5 hours = <<12/1.5=8>>8 miles/hour.\n#### 8"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To find the average speed in miles per hour, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Determine the total distance traveled.\n2. Determine the total time taken.\n3. Use the formula for average speed: \\(\\text{Average Speed} = \\frac{\\text{Total Distance}}{\\text{Total Time}}\\).\n\nStep 1: Determine the total distance traveled.\nThe problem states that you run 12 miles in 90 minutes. Since the distance is already given in miles, we don't need to convert it to any other unit.\n\nStep 2: Determine the total time taken.\nThe problem states that the time taken is 90 minutes. To convert this time into hours, we use the fact that 1 hour = 60 minutes. Therefore, 90 minutes is equivalent to:\n\\[ \\frac{90}{60} = 1.5 \\text{ hours} \\]\n\nStep 3: Use the formula for average speed.\nThe formula for average speed is:\n\\[ \\text{Average Speed} = \\frac{\\text{Total Distance}}{\\text{Total Time}} \\]\nSubstituting the values we have:\n\\[ \\text{Average Speed} = \\frac{12 \\text{ miles}}{1.5 \\text{ hours}} \\]\n\\[ \\text{Average Speed} = 8 \\text{ miles per hour} \\]\n\nTherefore, the average speed is \\(\\boxed{8}\\).",
